From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:29:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(git): honor core.sshCommand instead of forcing
 batch-mode ssh

App-managed git exported GIT_SSH_COMMAND='ssh -o BatchMode=yes' whenever the
variable was unset. Git gives that variable precedence over core.sshCommand, so a
user's configured ssh wrapper (key routing, proxies, 1Password-style agents) was
silently bypassed and private clones failed that work in a terminal.

Probe the effective core.sshCommand for the invocation's cwd (through git itself, so
includes and per-repo config apply; cached briefly) and only add the batch-mode
default when neither it nor GIT_SSH_COMMAND picks an ssh command. Prompting stays
disabled either way via GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 and the empty askpass variables.

Fixes generalaction/emdash#3345

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
